From: Fabian Affolter <fabian.affolter@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove add_hookspecs call incompatible with pluggy >= 1.4

pluggy 1.4 introduced a ValueError when add_hookspecs finds no hook
specifications in the given module or class. The AdditionalLicensePluginManager
decorates the plugin base class (not individual methods) with HookspecMarker,
which pluggy no longer recognises, causing the import to fail.

The plugincode upstream SimplePluginManager (which this class mirrors) never
called add_hookspecs, so removing this call restores parity with that design.

--- a/src/licensedcode/additional_license_location_provider.py
+++ b/src/licensedcode/additional_license_location_provider.py
@@ -77,7 +77,6 @@ class AdditionalLicensePluginManager(object):
         self.manager = PluggyPluginManager(project_name=project_name)
         self.entrypoint = entrypoint
         self.plugin_base_class = plugin_base_class
-        self.manager.add_hookspecs(sys.modules[project_name])

         # set to True once this manager is initialized by running its setup()
         self.initialized = False
